{
  "_comment": "Map tile catalog (real data drives the schema). Each tile carries an integer `tile_id` (the identity used by every map data file), display `name`, `walkable` flag, RGB fallback `color`, and `sprite` key. Optional `flags` carry lighting metadata. Optional `interaction_type` + `interaction_data` drive tile interactions: \"shop\" (data is a Counter id), \"sign\" (data is the sign text), \"spawn\" (data is a spawn template id). v1 keyed records by stringified tile id; v2 flattens into an array and the integer `tile_id` is the cross-reference. Some v1 names collide (two \"Door\" entries) so the text `id` appends the tile_id to keep ids unique. Sparse id space (gaps at 15–19, 30–31, 40–42, etc.) is intentional — historical churn from the Python era; renumbering would touch every map file.",
